    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a8a223b6-fa5d-5958-9fe2-3c5feb886bc5",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\nx=3\\sin\\theta,\\qquad y=7\\cos\\theta,\\\\\n0\\le \\theta<2\\pi,\n\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$?\n\nThe range of $x$ is {{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x\\le$ {{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is {{field-4}} $\\le y$ {{field-5}} {{field-6}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nOver the full turn, $\\sin\\theta$ attains both $-1$ and $1$, including at permitted parameter values.\n\nMultiply by $3$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\sin\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n-3 &\\le 3\\sin\\theta\\le 3 \\\\\n-3 &\\le x\\le 3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-3\\le x\\le 3$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nOver the full turn, $\\cos\\theta$ attains both $-1$ and $1$, including at permitted parameter values.\n\nMultiply by $7$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n-7 &\\le 7\\cos\\theta\\le 7 \\\\\n-7 &\\le y\\le 7.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-7\\le y\\le 7$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value.",
