    "question": {
      ":question/id": "69495e22-a7e2-5d3c-ad05-9cd4bda837dd",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\nx=5\\sin\\theta-3,\\qquad y=-3\\cos\\theta+2,\\\\\n0\\le \\theta<2\\pi,\n\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$?\n\nThe range of $x$ is {{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x\\le$ {{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is {{field-4}} $\\le y$ {{field-5}} {{field-6}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nOver the full turn, $\\sin\\theta$ attains both $-1$ and $1$, including at permitted parameter values.\n\nMultiply by $5$ and translate by $-3$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\sin\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n-5 &\\le 5\\sin\\theta\\le 5 \\\\\n-8 &\\le 5\\sin\\theta-3\\le 2 \\\\\n-8 &\\le x\\le 2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-8\\le x\\le 2$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nOver the full turn, $\\cos\\theta$ attains both $-1$ and $1$, including at permitted parameter values.\n\nMultiplying by $-3$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $2$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n3 &\\ge-3\\cos\\theta\\ge-3 \\\\\n5 &\\ge-3\\cos\\theta+2\\ge-1 \\\\\n-1 &\\le y\\le 5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $-1\\le y\\le 5$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value.",
