    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8c3e15f5-1ad4-527a-87eb-bba68e34d0ee",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\nx=-3\\cos\\theta+3,\\qquad y=-2\\sin\\theta+3,\\\\\n\\frac{\\pi}{2}<\\theta\\le 2\\pi,\n\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$? Use $<$ or $\\le$ in the comparison blanks.\n\nThe range of $x$ is {{field-1}} {{field-2}} $x$ {{field-3}} {{field-4}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is {{field-5}} {{field-6}} $y$ {{field-7}} {{field-8}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=\\pi$ gives $\\cos\\theta=-1$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\cos\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\cos\\theta=1$ (included).\n\nThe value $-1$ is attained at $\\theta=\\pi$.\n\nThe value $1$ is attained at $\\theta=2\\pi$.\n\nMultiplying by $-3$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $3$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\cos\\theta\\le 1 \\\\\n3 &\\ge-3\\cos\\theta\\ge-3 \\\\\n6 &\\ge-3\\cos\\theta+3\\ge0 \\\\\n0 &\\le x\\le 6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $0\\le x\\le 6$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\nCheck the quarter-turn points in the parameter interval and its endpoint limits: $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=1$ (excluded endpoint); $\\theta=\\pi$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included); $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$ gives $\\sin\\theta=-1$ (included); $\\theta=2\\pi$ gives $\\sin\\theta=0$ (included).\n\nThe value $-1$ is attained at $\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$.\n\nThe value $1$ is approached at an excluded endpoint and is not attained elsewhere in the interval.\n\nMultiplying by $-2$ reverses both comparisons; translate by $3$, then write the bounds in increasing order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-1 &\\le \\sin\\theta<1 \\\\\n2 &\\ge-2\\sin\\theta>-2 \\\\\n5 &\\ge-2\\sin\\theta+3>1 \\\\\n1 &<y\\le 5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $1<y\\le 5$.\n\nContinuity gives every value between the stated bounds. The coordinate extrema need not occur at the same parameter value.",
